cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Testing the Fluorescence Advantage: Solar-Induced Fluorescence as an Early Indicator of Agricultural Drought Stress in Marathwada, Maharashtra"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maske"
    given-names: "Sakshi D."
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/GREEN_ALIBI"
url: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/GREEN_ALIBI"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21762501"
    description: "Zenodo archive of GREEN ALIBI v1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21762501"
abstract: >-
  A satellite remote-sensing study testing whether Solar-Induced Fluorescence
  (SIF), a proxy for photosynthetic activity, registers agricultural drought
  stress measurably earlier than NDVI, the reflectance-based indicator
  currently underpinning India's drought declaration and PMFBY crop-insurance
  payout process. Using GOSIF v2 fluorescence data and cloud-screened MODIS
  NDVI over Marathwada, Maharashtra, across eight growing seasons (2015-2023,
  excluding 2021; two years, 2015 and 2018, meeting this study's own
  rainfall-anomaly drought threshold), a quantitative SIF-to-NDVI decline lag
  was calculated and independently corroborated by a second, methodologically
  distinct cross-correlation lag estimate and a case-resampling bootstrap
  uncertainty analysis. SIF's decline preceded NDVI's decline in seven of the
  eight years studied, with 2018 a genuine exception, but the hypothesis that
  drought severity amplifies this lag was not supported. Independent CHIRPS
  rainfall validation confirmed the drought/normal classification, and
  district-level spatial analysis found mean SIF and rainfall anomaly
  significantly correlated (Pearson r = 0.567, p < 0.001, n = 64
  district-years), a relationship further characterized via a Moran's I
  spatial-autocorrelation diagnostic showing rainfall consistently spatially
  clustered (8 of 8 years) and SIF clustered in about half of the years
  studied (4 of 8). A supplementary comparison against the one well-documented
  official government drought-declaration date available (2018) found both
  satellite indicators leading the official declaration by roughly seven to
  eight weeks.
keywords:
  - solar-induced fluorescence
  - remote sensing
  - drought monitoring
  - NDVI
  - agricultural stress
  - Marathwada
  - Google Earth Engine
  - crop insurance
  - PMFBY
  - spatial statistics
